\pard\qc\sa180\f1\fs36\b\cf1 Administrator Access and Deployment Prerequisites\par
\pard\qc\sa240\f0\fs22\b0\cf2 Power BI Lineage Explorer\par

\pard\sa120\f0\fs22\cf0
\b Purpose\b0\par
Please provision or confirm the following accounts, permissions, infrastructure, and configuration before the application is deployed. All access should follow least-privilege and organizational security policies. Passwords, private keys, and API keys must be delivered through the approved secret-management system and must not be entered directly in this document.\par

\pard\sa160\fs26\b\cf1 1. Power BI Premium Per User Account\b0\cf0\par
\pard\sa80\fs22 A Power BI account with a Premium Per User license is required for report inventory, semantic-model inspection, report-definition retrieval, XMLA queries, and lineage analysis.\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\sa60\fs22 \bullet\tab Provide a dedicated Power BI user account, or approve the named application user account.\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\sa60\fs22 \bullet\tab Assign a Microsoft Power BI Premium Per User license to the account.\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\sa60\fs22 \bullet\tab Grant access to every required report workspace and every workspace containing a connected or upstream semantic model.\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\sa60\fs22 \bullet\tab Grant Build and Read access to the required semantic models. Contributor or higher workspace access may be required when report-definition export or detailed metadata retrieval is used.\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\sa60\fs22 \bullet\tab Confirm that tenant settings permit the required Power BI and Fabric API operations, report-definition or PBIX download where applicable, XMLA endpoint access, and cross-workspace semantic-model discovery.\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\sa60\fs22 \bullet\tab Provide the Microsoft Entra tenant ID and account UPN through the approved configuration process.\par
\pard\sa80\fs22\b Acceptance check:\b0 The account can sign in, list the authorized workspaces and reports, read required semantic models, and retrieve available report-definition and XMLA metadata.\par

\pard\sa160\fs26\b\cf1 2. Snowflake Service Account and Object-Creation Access\b0\cf0\par
\pard\sa80\fs22 A Snowflake service account is required for source-data lineage, metadata queries, and creation of approved application database objects.\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\sa60\fs22 \bullet\tab Create a dedicated non-personal Snowflake service account. Key-pair authentication or an approved secret-vault integration is preferred.\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\sa60\fs22 \bullet\tab Create or assign a least-privilege Snowflake role for the application.\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\sa60\fs22 \bullet\tab Provide USAGE on the required warehouse, database, and schema.\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\sa60\fs22 \bullet\tab Grant the role the approved CREATE privileges needed for application objects, such as tables, views, procedures, and functions, within a designated application schema.\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\sa60\fs22 \bullet\tab Grant read access to the required source metadata, information schema views, and lineage-related objects.\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\sa60\fs22 \bullet\tab Confirm network policy, firewall, DNS, and allow-list access from the Windows deployment server to the Snowflake account.\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\sa60\fs22 \bullet\tab Provide the account identifier, authentication method, role, warehouse, database, schema, and approved secret location.\par
\pard\sa80\fs22\b Acceptance check:\b0 The service account can connect from the deployment host, query authorized metadata, and create the approved objects inside the designated application schema.\par

\pard\sa160\fs26\b\cf1 3. Windows Deployment Dependencies\b0\cf0\par
\pard\sa80\fs22 The application requires a supported Windows environment because XMLA and certain Power BI semantic-model operations depend on Windows components.\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\sa60\fs22 \bullet\tab Provide a supported 64-bit Windows Server or Windows host for deployment.\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\sa60\fs22 \bullet\tab Install a supported 64-bit Python runtime and the project dependencies. Python 3.11 is the current project baseline.\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\sa60\fs22 \bullet\tab Install the required Microsoft Analysis Services or MSOLAP provider and Windows Python integration dependencies used for XMLA access.\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\sa60\fs22 \bullet\tab Create or approve a Windows service account with permission to run the application and read its secured configuration.\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\sa60\fs22 \bullet\tab Allow outbound HTTPS access to Microsoft Entra, Power BI, Fabric, Snowflake, and Anthropic endpoints.\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\sa60\fs22 \bullet\tab Configure corporate TLS certificates or an approved CA bundle when HTTPS inspection is enabled. Certificate verification must remain enabled.\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\sa60\fs22 \bullet\tab Approve the application port or reverse-proxy configuration and configure automatic startup, logging, monitoring, and restart behavior.\par
\pard\sa80\fs22\b Acceptance check:\b0 The application starts under the approved Windows service account, reaches all external services, and can load the MSOLAP/XMLA dependencies without errors.\par

\pard\sa160\fs26\b\cf1 4. Claude Configuration and Session-Linked Agents\b0\cf0\par
\pard\sa80\fs22 Claude access is required for the application's PowerAI analysis and agent-assisted lineage features.\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\sa60\fs22 \bullet\tab Provide an approved Anthropic or Claude API key through the organization's secret-management system.\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\sa60\fs22 \bullet\tab Confirm the target environment, such as Development, Test, UAT, or Production, and provide the environment-specific configuration.\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\sa60\fs22 \bullet\tab Confirm the approved Claude model, API endpoint if organization-specific, usage limits, rate limits, and cost controls.\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\sa60\fs22 \bullet\tab Provide or approve the agent definitions, agent names, roles, instructions, and tools enabled for the environment.\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\sa60\fs22 \bullet\tab Confirm which agents must be linked to each user session and how the session-to-agent mapping is persisted, expired, and audited.\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\sa60\fs22 \bullet\tab Confirm that session isolation prevents one user's conversation, cached lineage information, or agent state from appearing in another user's session.\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\sa60\fs22 \bullet\tab Provide the secret names or vault references used by the application. Do not send the API key in email, chat, tickets, or this document.\par
\pard\sa80\fs22\b Acceptance check:\b0 The application can initialize the approved Claude model, create or resolve the configured agents, retain them for the correct session, and isolate agent state between users.\par

\pard\sa180\fs26\b\cf1 Administrator Completion Checklist\b0\cf0\par
\pard\li180\sa60\fs22 [ ] Power BI PPU account and license assigned\par
\pard\li180\sa60\fs22 [ ] Power BI/Fabric tenant settings and workspace permissions confirmed\par
\pard\li180\sa60\fs22 [ ] Snowflake service account, role, warehouse, database, and schema provisioned\par
\pard\li180\sa60\fs22 [ ] Snowflake object-creation and metadata-read privileges validated\par
\pard\li180\sa60\fs22 [ ] Windows deployment host and service account prepared\par
\pard\li180\sa60\fs22 [ ] Python, MSOLAP/XMLA, certificates, network access, and application hosting configured\par
\pard\li180\sa60\fs22 [ ] Claude key stored securely and environment configuration approved\par
\pard\li180\sa60\fs22 [ ] Claude agents and session-linking rules approved and validated\par

